### 5.2.12.4 Command Completion

Upon completion of the Get Log Page command, the controller posts a completion queue entry to the Admin Completion Queue. Get Log Page command specific status values are defined in Figure 321.

### Figure 321: Get Log Page – Command Specific Status Values

| Value | Definition |
|-------|-------------|
| 9h    | Invalid Log Page: The log page indicated is invalid or not supported. This error condition is also returned if a reserved log page is requested. Controllers compliant with NVM Express Base Specification revision 2.2 and earlier may return Invalid Field in Command for this condition. |
| 29h   | I/O Command Set Not Supported: The specified I/O Command Set is not supported by the controller. |

### 5.2.13 Identify command

#### 5.2.13.1 Identify command overview

The Identify command returns a data buffer that describes information about the NVM subsystem, the domain, the controller or the namespace(s). The data structure is 4,096 bytes in size.

The Identify command uses the Data Pointer, Command Dword 10, Command Dword 11, and Command Dword 14 fields. All other command specific fields are reserved.

### Figure 322: Identify – Data Pointer

| Bits | Description |
|------|-------------|
| 127:00 | Data Pointer (DPTR): This field specifies the start of the data buffer. Refer to Figure 92 for the definition of this field. If using PRPs, this field shall not be a pointer to a PRP List as the data buffer may not cross more than one page boundary. |
