| 31:11 | Reserved |
| 10   | Enter Media Verification State (EMVS): If this bit is set to ‘1’, then the Media Verification state shall be entered if sanitize processing completes successfully (i.e., the Global Data Erased (GDE) bit is set to ‘1’ (refer to Figure 302)). If this bit is cleared to ‘0’, then this bit shall have no effect. If the SANACT field does not specify starting an NVM subsystem sanitize operation (i.e., is set to any value other than 010b, 011b, or 100b), then this bit shall be ignored by the controller. |
