| 37h   | Invalid Controller Data Queue: This error indicates: |
|       | • that the specified Controller Data Queue Identifier is invalid for the controller processing the command; or |
|       | • the controller associated with the Controller Data Queue specified by the Controller Data Queue Identifier is already logging user data changes. |
| 38h   | Not Enough Resources: This error indicates that there are not enough resources in the controller to process the command successfully. |
| 39h   | Controller Suspended: The requested operation is not allowed if the controller specified in the Controller Identifier field is suspended by a Migration Send command (refer to section 5.2.17.1.1). |

