After enabling RPMB Boot Partition Write Protection:

c) The default state for all Boot Partitions is the Write Locked state. In this state, a host may read a Boot Partition. In this state, the controller rejects attempts to write to a Boot Partition using the Firmware Commit command;
d) Each Boot Partition may be locked or unlocked independently using the corresponding bit in the Device Configuration Block data structure. A Boot Partition may be unlocked in the same command that enables RPMB Boot Partition Write Protection; and
e) If any Boot Partition has been unlocked, a power cycle or Controller Level Reset event results in that Boot Partition becoming write locked.

