<|ref|>title<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 372, 291, 388]]<|/det|>
#### 2.2.5 Authentication  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 396, 882, 470]]<|/det|>
NVMe over Fabrics supports both fabric secure channel that includes authentication (refer to section 8.3.5.1) and NVMe in- band authentication. An NVM subsystem may require a host to use fabric secure channel, NVMe in- band authentication, or both. The Discovery Service indicates if fabric secure channel shall be used for an NVM subsystem. The Connect response indicates if NVMe in- band authentication shall be used with that controller.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 476, 882, 551]]<|/det|>
A controller associated with an NVM subsystem that requires a fabric secure channel shall not accept any commands (i.e., Fabrics commands, Admin commands, or I/O commands) on an NVMe Transport until a secure channel is established. Following a Connect command, a controller that requires NVMe in- band authentication shall not accept any commands on the queue created by that Connect command other than authentication commands until NVMe in- band authentication has completed. Refer to section 8.3.5.  

<|ref|>sub_title<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 560, 318, 576]]<|/det|>
### 2.3 NVM Storage Model  

<|ref|>title<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 587, 300, 603]]<|/det|>
#### 2.3.1 Storage Entities  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 611, 515, 627]]<|/det|>
The NVM storage model includes the following entities:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 634, 600, 727]]<|/det|>
- NVM subsystems (refer to section 1.5.68);- Domains (refer to section 3.2.5);- Endurance Groups (refer to section 3.2.3);- Reclaim Groups and Reclaim Units (refer to section 3.2.4);- NVM Sets (refer to section 3.2.2); and- Namespaces (refer to section 3.2.1).  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 734, 318, 748]]<|/det|>
As illustrated in this section:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 756, 748, 787]]<|/det|>
- each domain is contained in a single NVM subsystem;- each Endurance Group is contained in a single domain and may contain either:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[202, 794, 450, 823]]<|/det|>
- one or more NVM Sets; or- one or more Reclaim Groups;  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 831, 883, 906]]<|/det|>
- each NVM Set is contained in a single Endurance Group and each namespace is contained in a single NVM Set. Each Media Unit is contained in a single Endurance Group; and- each Reclaim Group is contained in a single Endurance Group, each Reclaim Unit is contained in a Reclaim Group, and each namespace is contained in an Endurance Group within one or more Reclaim Units of the Reclaim Groups in that Endurance Group.
