<table><tr><td>Bits</td><td>Type</td><td>Reset¹</td><td>Description</td></tr><tr><td>31:07</td><td>RO</td><td>0h</td><td>Reserved</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="5">06</td><td rowspan="5">RO</td><td rowspan="5">HwInit</td><td>Shutdown Type (ST): If CSTS.SHST is set to a non-zero value, then this bit indicates the type of shutdown reported by CSTS.SHST.<br>If this bit is set to &#x27;1&#x27;, then CSTS.SHST is reporting the state of an NVM Subsystem Shutdown and this bit remains set to &#x27;1&#x27; until an NVM Subsystem Reset occurs.</td></tr><tr><td>If this bit is cleared to &#x27;0&#x27;, then CSTS.SHST is reporting the state of a controller shutdown.<br>An NVM Subsystem Reset shall clear this bit to &#x27;0&#x27;. All other Controller Level Resets shall not change the value of this bit.<br>If CSTS.SHST is cleared to 00b, then this bit should be ignored by the host.</td></tr><tr><td></td></tr><tr><td></td></tr><tr><td></td></tr></table>
