refer to Figure 704) then the controller is not able to start a sanitize operation and the command requesting the sanitize operation is aborted as specified in section 8.1.26.1.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 125, 674, 142]]<|/det|>
If a division event occurs during a sanitize operation, then that division event:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 148, 883, 223]]<|/det|>
may prevent successful completion of that sanitize operation as specified in section 8.1.26 (e.g., the division prevents access to some objects in the scope of the sanitize operation, refer to Figure 704, and those objects have not already been sanitized by that sanitize operation); or may not affect the sanitize operation (i.e., if the sanitize operation is able to be processed successfully as described in section 8.1.26).  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 229, 883, 275]]<|/det|>
