#### 3.6.3.1 NVM Subsystem Shutdown in a Single Domain NVM Subsystem  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 401, 883, 431]]<|/det|>
A normal shutdown on all controllers within the NVM subsystem (i.e., normal NVM Subsystem Shutdown) is initiated by:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[146, 437, 883, 483]]<|/det|>
a host writing the value 4E726D6Ch ("Nrml") to NSSD.NSSC when CAP.CPS is set to 11b; or issuing an NVMe-MI Shutdown command to a Management Endpoint (refer to the NVM Express Management Interface Specification) specifying a normal shutdown.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 489, 754, 505]]<|/det|>
