<|ref|>title<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 292, 491, 304]]<|/det|>
# 4.5 Identifier Format and Layout (Informative)

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 318, 883, 346]]<|/det|>
This section provides guidance for proper implementation of various identifiers defined in the Identify Controller, Identify Namespace, and Namespace Identification Descriptor data structures.

<|ref|>title<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 356, 633, 369]]<|/det|>
# 4.5.1 PCI Vendor ID (VID) and PCI Subsystem Vendor ID (SSVID)

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 380, 883, 423]]<|/det|>
The PCI Vendor ID (VID, bytes 01:00) and PCI Subsystem Vendor ID (SSVID, bytes 03:02) are defined in the Identify Controller data structure. The values are assigned by the PCI SIG. Each identifier is a 16-bit number in little endian format.

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 432, 188, 444]]<|/det|>
Example:

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 455, 315, 468]]<|/det|>
·VID = ABCDh; and

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 471, 295, 483]]<|/det|>
·SSVID = 1234h.

<|ref|>table_caption<|/ref|><|det|>[[222, 500, 773, 513]]<|/det|>
Figure 127: PCI Vendor ID (VID) and PCI Subsystem Vendor ID (SSVID)

<|ref|>table<|/ref|><|det|>[[256, 522, 745, 553]]<|/det|>

<table><tr><td>Bytes</td><td>00</td><td>01</td><td>02</td><td>03</td></tr><tr><td>Value</td><td>CDh</td><td>ABh</td><td>34h</td><td>12h</td></tr></table>

<|ref|>title<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 563, 519, 576]]<|/det|>
# 4.5.2 Serial Number (SN) and Model Number (MN)

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 588, 883, 629]]<|/det|>
The Serial Number (SN, bytes 23:04) and Model Number (MN, bytes 63:24) are defined in the Identify Controller data structure. The values are ASCII strings assigned by the vendor. Each identifier is in big endian format.

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 639, 446, 652]]<|/det|>
Example (Value shown as ASCII characters):

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 661, 299, 673]]<|/det|>
·SN="SN1"; and

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 677, 259, 688]]<|/det|>
·MN="M2".

<|ref|>table_caption<|/ref|><|det|>[[280, 706, 718, 719]]<|/det|>
Figure 128: Serial Number (SN) and Model Number (MN)

<|ref|>table<|/ref|><|det|>[[135, 728, 860, 761]]<|/det|>

<table><tr><td>Bytes</td><td>04</td><td>05</td><td>06</td><td>23 to 07</td><td>24</td><td>25</td><td>63 to 26</td></tr><tr><td>Value</td><td>53h('S')</td><td>4Eh('N')</td><td>31h('1')</td><td>20h('')</td><td>4Dh('M')</td><td>32h('2')</td><td>20h('')</td></tr></table>

<|ref|>title<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 770, 375, 782]]<|/det|>
# 4.5.3 IEEE OUI Identifier (IEEE)

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 794, 883, 821]]<|/det|>
The IEEE OUI Identifier (OUI, bytes 75:73) is defined in the Identify Controller data structure. The value is assigned by the IEEE Registration Authority. The identifier is in little endian format.

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 831, 188, 842]]<|/det|>
Example:

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 853, 304, 865]]<|/det|>
·OUI=ABCDEFh.
