<|ref|>title<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 167, 488, 181]]<|/det|>
# 4.5.4 IEEE Extended Unique Identifier (EUI64)

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 192, 883, 250]]<|/det|>
The IEEE Extended Unique Identifier (EUI64, bytes 127:120) is defined in the Identify Namespace data structure. Tutorials are available at https://standards.ieee.org/develop/regauth/tut/index.html. IEEE defines three formats that may be used in this field: MA-L, MA-M, and MA-S. The examples in this section use the MA-L format.

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 258, 507, 271]]<|/det|>
The MA-L format is defined as a string of eight octets:

<|ref|>table_caption<|/ref|><|det|>[[240, 287, 757, 301]]<|/det|>
Figure 130: IEEE Extended Unique Identifier (EUI64), MA-L Format

<|ref|>table<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 310, 854, 340]]<|/det|>

<table><tr><td>EUI[0]</td><td>EUI[1]</td><td>EUI[2]</td><td>EUI[3]</td><td>EUI[4]</td><td>EUI[5]</td><td>EUI[6]</td><td>EUI[7]</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>OUI</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td colspan="3">Extension Identifier</td></tr></table>

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 355, 883, 383]]<|/det|>
EUI64 is defined in big endian format. The OUI field differs from the OUI Identifier which is in little endian format as described in section 4.5.3.

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 392, 188, 404]]<|/det|>
Example:

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[144, 415, 405, 427]]<|/det|>
· OUI Identifier = ABCDEFh; and

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[144, 430, 439, 442]]<|/det|>
· Extension Identifier = 0123456789h.

<|ref|>table_caption<|/ref|><|det|>[[240, 459, 757, 473]]<|/det|>
