If a host does not set the LBA Format Extension Enable (LBAFEE) field to 1h in the Host Behavior Support feature (refer to section 5.2.26.1.14), then the 0h value of the LBAFEE field disables any I/O Command Set specific format that requires the LBAFEE field to be set to 1h (refer to the applicable NVM Express I/O Command Set specification). If a Format NVM command specifies a format that is disabled (e.g., the LBAFEE field is cleared to 0h), then the controller shall abort that Format NVM command with a status code of Invalid Namespace or Format.

