<|ref|>title<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 466, 602, 483]]<|/det|>
#### 5.2.12.1.8 Telemetry Host-Initiated (Log Page Identifier 07h)  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 490, 883, 624]]<|/det|>
This log page consists of a header (i.e., bytes 511:0 of the log page) describing the log and zero or more Telemetry Data Blocks (refer to section 8.1.29). The header shall always be available even if there is no Telemetry Host- Initiated Data available. All Telemetry Data Blocks are 512 bytes in size. The controller shall initiate a capture of internal controller- scoped or NVM subsystem- scoped state to this log page if the controller processes a Get Log Page command for this log with the Create Telemetry Host- Initiated Data bit set to &#x27;1&#x27; in the Log Specific Parameter field. The scope of the saved state is determined by the value in the Telemetry Host- Initiated Scope field. If the host specifies a Log Page Offset Lower value that is not a multiple of 512 bytes in the Get Log Page command for this log page, then the controller shall abort the command with a status code of Invalid Field in Command.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 629, 883, 660]]<|/det|>
The Log Specific Parameter field in Command Dword 10 (refer to Figure 201) for this log page is defined in Figure 217.  

<|ref|>table<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 697, 882, 727]]<|/det|>
<|ref|>table_caption<|/ref|><|det|>[[243, 673, 754, 689]]<|/det|>
Figure 217: Telemetry Host-Initiated Log Specific Parameter Field   

<table><tr><td>Bits</td><td>Description</td></tr><tr><td>14:12</td><td>Reserved</td></tr></table>
