) + 4</td><td>Command Completion Dword 0 (CCDWO): If the Logged Command Completion Dword 0 bit is set to ‘1’, then this field contains the Dword 0 value from the Set Features command completion. If the Logged Command Completion Dword 0 bit is cleared to ‘0’, then this field is not logged.</td><td></td></tr></table>  

<|ref|>title<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 578, 648, 595]]<|/det|>
#### 5.2.12.1.14.2.12 Telemetry Log Create Event (Event Type 0Ch)  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 603, 883, 649]]<|/det|>
A Telemetry Log Create event may be created if the controller determines that a Telemetry Host- Initiated log page (refer to section 5.2.12.1.8) or that a Telemetry Controller- Initiated log page (refer to section 5.2.12.1.9) has been generated.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 654, 711, 671]]<|/det|>
The Telemetry Log Create Event shall set the Persistent Event Log Event Header:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 678, 420, 709]]<|/det|>
Event Type field to 0Ch; and Event Type Revision Field to 01h.  

<|ref|>table<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 746, 881, 804]]<|/det|>
