Figure 251: Telemetry Log Create Event Data Format (Event Type 0Ch)   

<table><tr><td>Bytes</td><td>Description</td></tr><tr><td>511:00</td><td>Telemetry Initiated Log (TIL): Contains a copy of the values from the first 512 bytes of the Telemetry Host-Initiated log page (refer to Figure 218) or the first 512 bytes of the Telemetry Controller-Initiated log page (refer to Figure 220).</td></tr></table>  

<|ref|>title<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 812, 628, 828]]<|/det|>
#### 5.2.12.1.14.2.13 Thermal Excursion Event (Event Type 0Dh)  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 836, 883, 867]]<|/det|>
A Thermal Excursion event shall be recorded in the Persistent Event Log if the Composite Temperature has transitioned from a temperature that is less than:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 874, 883, 905]]<|/det|>
the WCTEMP, if any, (refer to Figure 328) to a temperature that is greater than or equal to the WCTEMP, if any; or
