The format of the Placement Identifier used in the Data Placement Directive (refer to section 8.1.9.4) for a specific FDP configuration is dependent on the number of Reclaim Groups supported by the FDP configuration in use and the number of bits allocated for the Reclaim Group Identifier field. If the NRG field (refer to Figure 287) is set to 1h indicating that there is only one Reclaim Group and zero bits are allocated to the Reclaim Group Identifier (i.e., the RGIF field (refer to Figure 287) is cleared to 0h), then the format of the Placement Identifier is defined in Figure 289. If one or more bits are allocated to the Reclaim Group Identifier (i.e., the RGIF field is non-zero), then the format of the Placement Identifier is defined in Figure 290.

