<|ref|>title<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 388, 330, 404]]<|/det|>
#### 5.2.12.12.31 Host Events  

<|ref|>title<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 413, 693, 430]]<|/det|>
#### 5.2.12.12.31.1 Reclaim Unit Not Fully Written To Capacity (Event Type 0h)  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 437, 883, 483]]<|/det|>
This FDP event indicates that the Reclaim Unit Handle reported in the Placement Identifier (refer to Figure 289 and Figure 290) was modified to reference a different Reclaim Unit due to an I/O Management Send command issued by the host prior to the previously referenced Reclaim Unit being written to capacity.  

<|ref|>title<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 491, 628, 507]]<|/det|>
#### 5.2.12.12.31.2 Reclaim Unit Time Limit Exceeded (Event Type 1h)  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 515, 883, 560]]<|/det|>
This FDP event indicates that the capacity of a Reclaim Unit was not completely written within the time period defined in the Estimated Reclaim Unit Time Limit field (refer to Figure 287) due to the controller modifying the Reclaim Unit Handle to reference a different Reclaim Unit.  

<|ref|>title<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 569, 778, 585]]<|/det|>
#### 5.2.12.12.31.3 Controller Level Reset Modified Reclaim Unit Handles (Event Type 2h)  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 594, 883, 625]]<|/det|>
This FDP event indicates that one or more Reclaim Unit Handles were modified to reference a different Reclaim Unit due to a Controller Level Reset.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 631, 764, 647]]<|/det|>
In the FDP event, the NSID field is reserved and the Placement Identifier field is reserved.  

<|ref|>title<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 655, 574, 671]]<|/det|>
#### 5.2.12.12.31.4 Invalid Placement Identifier (Event Type 3h)  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 680, 883, 710]]<|/det|>
This FDP event indicates that a write command specified an invalid Placement Identifier (refer to Figure 289 and Figure 290) due to an invalid Placement Handle or an invalid Reclaim Group Identifier.  

<|ref|>title<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 719, 372, 735]]<|/det|>
#### 5.2.12.12.32 Controller Events  

<|ref|>title<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 743, 513, 760]]<|/det|>
#### 5.2.12.12.32.1 Media Reallocated (Event Type 80h)  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 768, 883, 813]]<|/det|>
This FDP event indicates that user data contained in a Reclaim Unit was written by the host specifying a Reclaim Unit Handle with a Reclaim Unit Handle type of Initially Isolated and was moved by the controller to a different Reclaim Unit (e.g., controller performed garbage collection).  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 820, 883, 865]]<|/det|>
The Event Type Specific field is I/O Command Set specific. Refer to the applicable NVM Express I/O Command Set specification to determine if this log page is supported and the definition of the Event Type Specific field for this FDP event.  

<|ref|>title<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 873, 675, 890]]<|/det|>
#### 5.2.12.12.32.2 Implicitly Modified Reclaim Unit Handle (Event Type 81h)
2025-12-21 10:51:40 - ocr_processor - [32mINFO[0m - [deepseek_ocr.py:175] - Processing image start: out/output_png/0313_page.png
2025-12-21 10:51:44 - ocr_processor - [32mINFO[0m - [deepseek_ocr.py:182] - Processing image end: <|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 90, 883, 134]]<|/det|>
This FDP event indicates that the controller modified a Reclaim Unit Handle to reference a different Reclaim Unit where that modification was not due to any host action (e.g., a write command that has a size greater than the remaining capacity of the initial Reclaim Unit being written).  

<|ref|>title<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 148, 575, 164]]<|/det|>
#### 5.2.12.1.33 Power Measurement (Log Page Identifier 25h)  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 173, 883, 203]]<|/det|>
The Power Measurement log page (refer to Figure 297) is used for the reporting of logged interval power measurements for the Power Measurement capability, including:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 210, 532, 256]]<|/det|>
the average of the interval power measurements; the maximum interval power measurement; and a histogram of the interval power measurements.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 263, 705, 279]]<|/det|>
The information in this log page shall be retained across power cycles and resets.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[116, 285, 452, 301]]<|/det|>
This log page is global to the NVM subsystem.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 307, 598, 322]]<|/det|>
Refer to section 8.1.19.1 for the usage of this log page by the host.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 329, 883, 374]]<|/det|>
The Power Histogram Descriptor is defined in Figure 298. In this log page, the Power Histogram Descriptors shall be listed in ascending order based on the power indicated by the Power Histogram Bin Lower Threshold (PHBLT) field.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 381, 133, 394]]<|/det|>
If:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 403, 883, 450]]<|/det|>
the Power Measurement Count (PMC) field is set to a non- zero value at the time this log page is read; and the Number of Power Histogram Descriptors Supported (NPHDS) field is set to a non- zero value,  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 457, 149, 470]]<|/det|>
then  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 478, 883, 583]]<|/det|>
the first Power Histogram Descriptor (i.e., Power Histogram Descriptor 0) shall have the Power Histogram Bin Lower Threshold (PHBLT) field set to 0 Watts; the last Power Histogram Descriptor (i.e., Power Histogram Descriptor NPHD- 1) shall contain the highest power in the PHBLT field with a non- zero value in the Power Histogram Bin Count (PHBC) field; and there shall be no gaps in the power ranges in the set of Power Histogram Descriptors returned (i.e. Power Histogram Descriptors with non- zero values in PHBC field are not packed together).  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 589, 883, 621]]<|/det|>
If the Power Measurement Count (PMC) field is cleared to Oh at the time this log page is read, then the Number of Power Histogram Descriptors (NPHD) field shall be cleared to Oh.  

