<table><tr><td>Bytes</td><td>Description</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Power Measurement Attributes (PMA): This field contains attributes of this log page.</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="10">3:2</td><td>Bits</td></tr><tr><td>Definition</td></tr><tr><td>Power Measurement Type (PMT): This field indicates the power measurement type for the interval power measurement data reported in this log page as defined in Figure 679. If the PMC field is cleared to 0h, then the host should ignore this field.</td></tr><tr><td>11:5</td></tr><tr><td>Reserved</td></tr><tr><td>Power Histogram Descriptor Overflow (PHD0): If this bit is set to &#x27;1&#x27;, then at least one interval power measurement (i.e., average of power measurement samples over one second, refer to section 8.1.19) collected for this log page is greater than the maximum power indicated by the last Power Histogram Descriptor (i.e., Power Histogram Descriptor NPHD-1) in this log page. If this bit is cleared to &#x27;0&#x27;, then no overflow has occurred.</td></tr><tr><td>Maximum Interval Power Timestamp Support (MIPWRTS): If this bit is set to &#x27;1&#x27;, then the NVM subsystem supports reporting a timestamp in the Maximum Interval Power Timestamp (MIPWRT) field. If this bit is cleared to &#x27;0&#x27;, then the NVM subsystem does not support reporting a timestamp in the MIPWRT field.</td></tr><tr><td>Estimated Power Flag (EPF): If this bit is set to &#x27;1&#x27;, then estimated power measurements are allowed to be used for the values reported in this log page. If this bit is cleared to &#x27;0&#x27;, then the values reported in this log page shall be based on measured power.</td></tr><tr><td>Non-Contiguous Power Data Flag (NCPDF): If this bit is set to &#x27;1&#x27;, then the data reported in this log page is based on non-contiguous interval power measurements (refer to section 8.1.19). If this bit is cleared to &#x27;0&#x27;, then the data reported in this log page is based on contiguous interval power measurements.</td></tr><tr><td>If the Power Measurement Count (PMC) field is cleared to 0h, then this bit shall be cleared to &#x27;0&#x27;.</td></tr><tr><td>Power Measurement Enable (PME): If this bit is set to &#x27;1&#x27;, then interval power measurements (refer to section 8.1.19) of the indicated power measurement type (i.e., PMT field) are being collected for this log page. If this bit is cleared to &#x27;0&#x27;, then no interval power measurements are being collected for this log page.</td></tr><tr><td>7:4</td><td>Size (SZE): This field indicates the size of this log page in bytes.</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="2">11:8</td><td>Power Measurement Count (PMC): This field indicates the current number of interval power measurements (i.e., average of power measurement samples over one second, refer to section 8.1.19) collected for this log page.</td></tr><tr><td>This field shall not wrap once the value FFFFFFFF is reached.</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>If:</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>a) a Set Features command specifying the Power Measurement feature with the Action field set to 1h (i.e., Start Power Measurements) is successfully completed (refer to section 5.2.26.1.27); or<br>b) no measurement has occurred (i.e., the PME bit in this log page has never been set to &#x27;1&#x27;) since time of manufacture,</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>then this field shall be cleared to 0h.</td></tr><tr><td>13:12</td><td>Number of Power Histogram Descriptors (NPHD): This field indicates the number of Power Histogram Descriptors in this log page.</td></tr><tr><td>15:14</td><td>Stop Measurement Time Remaining (SMTR): This field indicates the time remaining in minutes until the controller stops collecting interval power measurements (refer to section 8.1.19) for this log page. If this field is cleared to 0h, then no stop measurement time is specified.</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>If the PME bit is cleared to &#x27;0&#x27;, then this field shall be cleared to 0h.</td></tr></table>
