<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 285, 883, 404]]<|/det|>
The Get Log Page command returns a data buffer containing a log page formatted as defined in Figure 300. The NSID List, defined in Figure 300, is an ordered list of ascending NSIDs. If the controller is not able to report valid data (e.g., due to a division event that prevents accessing some of the sanitize status information), then the Get Log Page command shall be aborted with a status code of Controller Patching Error. If a Get Log Page command is aborted with a status code of Controller Patching Error, then submitting a subsequent Get Log Page command to a controller with a different domain identifier and requesting the same Sanitize Namespace Status List log page may be successful. If the controller is able to report valid data, then this log page shall contain valid data whenever CSTS.RDY is set to '1'.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 408, 883, 440]]<|/det|>
If the Sanitize Namespace command is supported by the controller, then this log page shall be supported by the controller.  

<|ref|>table<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 476, 880, 710]]<|/det|>
<|ref|>table_caption<|/ref|><|det|>[[288, 453, 707, 470]]<|/det|>
