was processing the associated operation for this entry.</td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td>If this bit is cleared to &#x27;0&#x27;, then no information is available on whether a CLR was initiated or was in progress on the Impacted Controller.</td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td>If the V bit is cleared to &#x27;0&#x27;, then this bit shall be cleared to &#x27;0&#x27;.</td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td>Validated (V): If this bit is set to &#x27;1&#x27;, then the Cross-Controller Reset operation identified the Impacted Controller and met all the preconditions for initiating a CLR on the Impacted Controller, i.e.:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td>• the Source Controller was authorized to cause the NVM subsystem to initiate a Cross-Controller Reset operation for the Impacted Controller (i.e., the operation associated with this entry is not prohibited by any NVM subsystem authorization or access control policy, refer to step 2 in section 8.3.3.1);</td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td>• the Source Controller and the Impacted Controller were associated with the same host, as indicated by the Host NQN;</td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td>• the value of the CIU field specified in the Cross-Controller Reset command that caused the NVM subsystem to initiate the associated operation for this entry was the same as the value of the CIU field in the Identify Controller data structure for the Impacted Controller; and</td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td>• the CIRN (i.e., the combination of the value of the CIRNL field and the value of the CIRNU field) specified in the Cross-Controller Reset command that caused the NVM subsystem to initiate the associated operation for this entry was the same as the value of CIRN field in the Identify Controller data structure for the Impacted Controller.</td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td>For more information on these conditions, refer to section 8.3.3.</td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td>If this bit is cleared to &#x27;0&#x27;, then at least one of the four conditions was not satisfied, or the associated operation for this entry was unable to determine whether all of these conditions were satisfied.</td><td></td></tr></table>
