<|ref|>title<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 536, 316, 552]]<|/det|>
#### 5.2.13 Identify command  

<|ref|>title<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 561, 402, 577]]<|/det|>
#### 5.2.13.1 Identify command overview  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 585, 883, 616]]<|/det|>
The Identify command returns a data buffer that describes information about the NVM subsystem, the domain, the controller or the namespace(s). The data structure is 4,096 bytes in size.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 622, 883, 652]]<|/det|>
The Identify command uses the Data Pointer, Command Dword 10, Command Dword 11, and Command Dword 14 fields. All other command specific fields are reserved.  

<|ref|>table<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 690, 881, 747]]<|/det|>
<|ref|>table_caption<|/ref|><|det|>[[364, 666, 631, 682]]<|/det|>
Figure 322: Identify - Data Pointer   

<table><tr><td>Bits</td><td>Description</td></tr><tr><td>127:00</td><td>Data Pointer (DPTR): This field specifies the start of the data buffer. Refer to Figure 92 for the definition of this field. If using PRPs, this field shall not be a pointer to a PRP List as the data buffer may not cross more than one page boundary.</td></tr></table>
