 Measurement capability (refer to section 8.1.19.1). If cleared to ‘0’, then the controller does not support the Power Measurement capability.</td></tr><tr><td>20</td><td>Power Limit Support (PLS): If this bit is set to ‘1’, then the controller supports the Power Limit feature (refer to section 5.2.26.1.25). If this bit is cleared to ‘0’, then the controller does not support the Power Limit feature.</td></tr><tr><td>19</td><td>Flexible Data Placement Support (FDPS): If this bit is set to ‘1’, then the controller supports the Flexible Data Placement capability (refer to section 8.1.11). If this bit is cleared to ‘0’, then the controller does not support the Flexible Data Placement capability.</td></tr><tr><td>18</td><td>If Fixed Capacity Management is supported (i.e., the FCM bit is set to ‘1’), then this bit shall be cleared to ‘0’.</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Reservations and Host Identifier Interaction (RHII): This bit indicates the reservations and Host Identifier interaction support for the controller.</td></tr><tr><td>Value</td><td>Definition</td></tr><tr><td>Ob</td><td>Not Reported</td></tr><tr><td>1b</td><td>The Host Identifier is required to be set to a non-zero value for a host to use reservations (refer to section 8.1.24).</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>HMB Restrict Non-Operational Power State Access (HMBR): If this bit is set to ‘1’, then the controller supports restricting HMB access in non-operational power states as defined in section 5.2.26.2.4. If this bit is cleared to ‘0’, then the controller does not support restricting HMB access in non-operational power states as defined by section 5.2.26.2.4.</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>MDTS and Size Limits Exclude Metadata (MEM): If this bit is set to ‘1’, then:</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>• The controller reported MDTS values do not include interleaved metadata.</td></tr></table>
