by the controller for use by the<br>Configurable Device Personality capability.<br>7:0 Bits Description<br>7:1 Reserved<br>HMAC-SHA-384 (HS3): If HMAC-SHA-384 is supported (refer to<br>0 RFC 6234), then this bit shall be set to '1'; otherwise, this bit shall be<br>cleared to '0'.</td></tr><tr><td></td></tr><tr><td></td></tr><tr><td>391:390</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>Maximum Unlimited Power (MUP): This field specifies the maximum power for power<br>state 0 that results from removal of a power limit (i.e., the maximum power is not limited).<br>If the Power Limit feature is not supported (i.e., the PLS bit in the CTRATT field is cleared to '0'), then the controller shall clear this field to 0h.<br>If the Power Limit feature is supported (i.e., the PLS bit in the CTRATT field is set to '1'), then the value in this field combined with the value of the MUPS field shall be equal to<br>the value of the Maximum Power (MP) field of the PSD0 field in the Identify Controller<br>data structure while the current value of the PLV attribute of that feature is cleared to 0h<br>(refer to section 5.2.26.1.25). If the Power Limit feature is supported and the current value<br>of the PLV attribute is not cleared to 0h, then the value of this field combined with the<br>value of the MUPS field shall indicate the value of the MP field that results from clearing<br>the current value of the PLV attribute to 0h. Refer to section 8.1.18.6.</td></tr></table>
