<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 283, 443, 299]]<|/det|>
If the controller supports selection of a UUID:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 305, 883, 365]]<|/det|>
a) by the Lockdown command; and  
b) by the Set Features command (refer to section 5.2.26 and section 8.1.30) and for the vendor specific Feature Identifier specified by the Opcode or Feature Identifier field, if the Scope field is set to 2h,  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 370, 733, 387]]<|/det|>
then Command Dword 14 (refer to Figure 354) is used to specify a UUID Index value.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 392, 501, 408]]<|/det|>
If the controller does not support selection of a UUID:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 415, 883, 475]]<|/det|>
a) by the Lockdown command;  
b) by the Set Features command; or  
c) for the vendor specific feature identifier specified by the Opcode or Feature Identifier field, if the Scope field is set to 2h,  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 480, 883, 511]]<|/det|>
then Command Dword 14 does not specify a UUID Index value. If the Scope field is not set to 2h, then UUID Index field is ignored.  

<|ref|>table<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 547, 882, 592]]<|/det|>
<|ref|>table_caption<|/ref|><|det|>[[321, 524, 675, 540]]<|/det|>
Figure 354: Lockdown - Command Dword 14   

<table><tr><td>Bits</td><td>Description</td></tr><tr><td>31:07</td><td>Reserved</td></tr><tr><td>06:00</td><td>UUID Index (UIDX): Refer to Figure 716.</td></tr></table>  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 597, 883, 628]]<|/det|>
If a controller processes a Lockdown command that specifies a command opcode or Feature Identifier that is:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 635, 883, 760]]<|/det|>
not indicated as being able to be prohibited from execution (refer to Figure 271), then that command shall be aborted with a status code of Prohibition of Command Execution Not Supported; or indicated as being able to be prohibited from execution (refer to Figure 271) but that command opcode or Feature Identifier is not supported on one of the interfaces specified in the Interface field (e.g., an Admin Submission Queue, a Management Endpoint) of that Lockdown command, then:  - that command should be aborted with a status code of Prohibition of Command Execution Not Supported; and  - that command may be aborted with a status code of Invalid Field in Command.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 767, 883, 812]]<|/det|>
If a controller processes this command with the Interface field set to 01b or 10b and the NVM subsystem does not contain a Management Endpoint, then the command shall be aborted with a status code of Invalid Field in Command.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 818, 883, 848]]<|/det|>
If a controller processes this command with the Interface field set to 00b or 01b and the Scope field is set to 4h, then the command shall be aborted with a status code of Invalid Field in Command.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 854, 883, 885]]<|/det|>
It is not an error to attempt to prohibit a command or Feature Identifier that is already prohibited from execution or allow a command or Feature Identifier that is already allowed to be executed.
