hether an asynchronous event<br>notification is reported for a Cross-Controller Reset Completed asynchronous event (refer to Figure<br>154). If this bit is set to '1' and this condition occurs, then the Cross-Controller Reset Completed<br>asynchronous event is reported. If this bit is cleared to '0', then the controller shall not report the Cross-Controller Reset Completed asynchronous event.</td></tr><tr><td>19</td><td>Allocated Namespace Attribute Notices (ANSAN): This bit determines whether an asynchronous<br>event notification is sent to the host for an Allocated Namespace Attribute Changed asynchronous<br>event (refer to Figure 154). If this bit is set to '1', then the Allocated Namespace Attribute Changed<br>asynchronous event is sent to the host when this condition occurs. If this bit is cleared to '0', then the<br>controller shall not send the Allocated Namespace Attribute Changed asynchronous event to the host.</td></tr></table>
