<|ref|>title<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 714, 652, 730]]<|/det|>
#### 5.2.26.1.24 Configurable Device Personality (Feature Identifier 22h)  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 738, 883, 783]]<|/det|>
This Feature controls the operation of the Configurable Device Personality (CDP) capability (refer to section 8.1.6). The Set Features command allows a host to change the settings of a device personality in the NVM subsystem and the Get Features command allows a host to discover the settings for a device personality.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 790, 883, 820]]<|/det|>
Figure 447 defines personalities that are able to be supported by an NVM subsystem. Each personality may have multiple configurations.  

<|ref|>table<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 858, 881, 904]]<|/det|>
