<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 217, 883, 248]]<|/det|>
This Feature configures settings specific to a particular controller interrupt vector. The settings are specified in Command Dword 11.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 254, 881, 284]]<|/det|>
By default, coalescing settings are enabled for each interrupt vector. Interrupt coalescing is not supported for the Admin Completion Queue.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 289, 881, 335]]<|/det|>
If a Get Features command is submitted for this Feature, the attributes specified in Figure 475 are returned in Dword 0 of the completion queue entry for that command for the Interrupt Vector specified in Command Dword 11.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 341, 881, 401]]<|/det|>
Prior to issuing a Set Features command that specifies this Feature, the host shall configure the specified Interrupt Vector with an I/O Completion Queue (refer to section 5.3.1). If the specified Interrupt Vector is invalid, or not associated with an existing I/O Completion Queue (refer to Figure 504), then the controller should abort the command with a status code of Invalid Field in Command.  

