<|ref|>title<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 179, 362, 195]]<|/det|>
#### 5.4.3.1 Command Completion  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 203, 883, 234]]<|/det|>
Upon completion of the Cross- Controller Reset command, the controller posts a CQE to the Admin Completion Queue indicating the status for the Cross- Controller Reset command.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 239, 881, 271]]<|/det|>
If the command completes successfully, Dword 0 of the CQE indicates information about the CrossController Reset operation as shown in Figure 527.  

<|ref|>table<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 308, 882, 556]]<|/det|>
<|ref|>table_caption<|/ref|><|det|>[[177, 284, 817, 301]]<|/det|>
Figure 527: Cross-Controller Reset Command - Completion Queue Entry Dword 0   

<table><tr><td>Bits</td><td>Description</td></tr><tr><td>31:03</td><td>Reserved</td></tr><tr><td>02</td><td>Controller Level Reset Initiated (CLRI): This bit has the same definition as the Controller Level Reset Initiated bit defined in Figure 305.<br>If the value of the IRS bit is set to &#x27;0&#x27;, the value of this bit is undefined.</td></tr><tr><td>01</td><td>Validated (V): This bit has the same definition as the Validated bit defined in Figure 305.<br>If the value of the IRS bit is set to &#x27;0&#x27;, the value of this bit is undefined.</td></tr><tr><td>00</td><td>Immediate Reset Successful (IRS): If this bit is set to &#x27;1&#x27;, then:<br>• the Cross-Controller Reset operation completed successfully as described in section 8.3.3;<br>• the Source Controller does not report a Cross-Controller Reset Completed asynchronous event (refer to Figure 154) for the Cross-Controller Reset operation caused to be initiated by this command; and<br>• the Source controller does not add an entry for the Cross-Controller Reset operation to the Cross-Controller Reset log page.<br>If this bit is cleared to &#x27;0&#x27;, then the Cross-Controller Reset operation was not completed successfully before this CQE was posted.</td></tr></table>  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 569, 883, 614]]<|/det|>
If the value of the ICID field in the Cross- Controller Reset command is the same as the controller ID of the Source Controller, the Source Controller shall abort the command with a status code of Invalid Field in Command. If:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[142, 620, 883, 668]]<|/det|>
the value of the ICID field in the Cross- Controller Reset command is the same as the value of the ICID field in a pre- existing entry in the Cross- Controller Reset log page; and the Cross- Controller Reset Status (CCRS) field in that entry is set to In Progress,  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 673, 810, 689]]<|/det|>
the controller shall abort the command with a status code of Cross- Controller Reset in Progress.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 694, 709, 711]]<|/det|>
Cross- Controller Reset command specific status values are defined in Figure 528.  

<|ref|>table<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 748, 882, 873]]<|/det|>
<|ref|>table_caption<|/ref|><|det|>[[220, 724, 773, 740]]<|/det|>
Figure 528: Cross-Controller Reset - Command Specific Status Values   

<table><tr><td>Value</td><td>Description</td></tr><tr><td>3Fh</td><td>Cross-Controller Reset in Progress: There is already an in-progress Cross-Controller Reset operation that this controller caused to be initiated for the Impacted Controller.</td></tr><tr><td>40h</td><td>Cross-Controller Reset Log Page Full: The controller has detected that the Cross-Controller Reset log page already contains the maximum number of entries (refer to Figure 304).</td></tr><tr><td>41h</td><td>Cross-Controller Reset Limit Exceeded: The controller has detected that the number of simultaneous in-progress Cross-Controller Reset operations this controller caused to be initiated is greater than or equal to the value indicated in the Cross-Controller Reset Limit field in the Identify Controller data structure (refer to Figure 328) of the Source Controller.</td></tr></table>
