#### 5.4.8.1 Manage Exported Namespace Management Operations  

<|ref|>title<|/ref|><|det|>[[137, 125, 624, 141]]<|/det|>
#### 5.4.8.1.1 Associate Namespace (Management Operation 01h)  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 149, 882, 209]]<|/det|>
The Associate Namespace operation of the Manage Exported Namespace command is used to create an association between an Exported Namespace ID (ENSID) and an Underlying Namespace; this command also associates the ENSID with an Exported NVM Subsystem identified by the Exported NVM Subsystem NQN.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 215, 882, 276]]<|/det|>
The Underlying Namespace to be associated with the Exported Namespace ID is returned in the Underlying Namespace List as an Underlying Namespace List Entry (refer to Figure 350) and identified with an Underlying Controller ID, Underlying NVM Subsystem, and Underlying Namespace ID combination. That information is specified in an Associate Namespace data structure (refer to Figure 552).  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 281, 882, 341]]<|/det|>
The Manage Exported Namespace command with an Associate Namespace operation does not attach the Exported Namespace to a controller. The Exported Namespace becomes an attached namespace when attached to a controller due to the processing of a Namespace Attachment command (refer to section 5.2.20).  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 346, 780, 363]]<|/det|>
The data pointer shall point to an Associate Namespace data structure (refer to Figure 552).  

<|ref|>table<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 400, 881, 578]]<|/det|>
<|ref|>table_caption<|/ref|><|det|>[[305, 376, 690, 392]]<|/det|>
Figure 552: Associate Namespace Data Structure   

<table><tr><td>Bytes</td><td>Description</td></tr><tr><td>31:00</td><td>Exported Namespace ID (ENSID): A valid and unassociated Exported NSID to be associated to an Underlying Namespace and associated with the specified Exported NVM Subsystem.</td></tr><tr><td>253:32</td><td>Exported NVM Subsystem NQN (ENSNQN): Identifies an existing Exported NVM Subsystem to be associated with the Exported Namespace ID.</td></tr><tr><td>285:254</td><td>Underlying Namespace ID (UNSID): An active Namespace ID to which Exported Namespace ID (ENSID) is to be associated. Refer to Figure 65 for the definition of NSID types and relationship to namespaces.</td></tr><tr><td>287:286</td><td>Underlying Controller ID (UCTRLID): Identifies the Underlying Controller used to access the specified Underlying Namespace.</td></tr><tr><td>543:288</td><td>Underlying NVM Subsystem NQN (UNSNQN): Identifies the Underlying NVM Subsystem which provides the Underlying Namespace to be associated with the Exported Namespace ID.</td></tr><tr><td>575:544</td><td>Reserved</td></tr></table>  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 590, 760, 606]]<|/det|>
The controller shall abort the command with a status code of Invalid Field in Command if:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[142, 612, 884, 824]]<|/det|>
a valid Exported Namespace ID is not specified in the Exported Namespace ID field in Figure 552; the Exported NVM Subsystem NQN field in Figure 552 does not refer to an existing Exported NVM Subsystem; the Underlying Namespace ID field in Figure 552 does not refer to an active Underlying Namespace ID; the Underlying Controller ID field in Figure 552 does not identify a controller contained in the Underlying NVM Subsystem specified by the Underlying NVM Subsystem NQN field; the Underlying Namespace specified by the Underlying Namespace ID field shown in Figure 552 is not attached to the controller specified by the Underlying Controller ID in the Underlying Controller ID field in Figure 552; the specified Underlying NVM Subsystem NQN field in Figure 552 does not refer to an existing Underlying NVM Subsystem; or the specified Underlying Namespace ID is not an allocated namespace in the Underlying NVM Subsystem NQN field in Figure 552.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 830, 882, 860]]<|/det|>
Upon successful completion of a Manage Exported Namespace command with an Associate Namespace operation:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[142, 867, 882, 899]]<|/det|>
the Exported NSID which is associated with an attached Underlying Namespace is an allocated namespace to the Exported NVM Subsystem. The Exported Namespace and the Underlying
