<|ref|>title<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 392, 652, 409]]<|/det|>
#### 5.4.9.1 Manage Exported NVM Subsystem Management Operations  

<|ref|>title<|/ref|><|det|>[[135, 417, 500, 433]]<|/det|>
#### 5.4.9.1.1 Delete (Management Operation 01h)  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 441, 883, 501]]<|/det|>
The Delete operation of the Manage Exported NVM Subsystem command is used to delete a specified Exported NVM Subsystem. The data buffer for the Delete operation of the Manage Exported NVM Subsystem command contains an NVM Subsystem NQN specifying the Exported NVM Subsystem to be deleted.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 507, 883, 538]]<|/det|>
The Management Operation Specific field in Command Dword 10 is reserved and not used by this operation.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 544, 883, 589]]<|/det|>
If a Manage Exported NVM Subsystem command is processed that specifies the Delete operation without specifying an existing Exported NVM Subsystem identified by the NVM Subsystem NQN (SUBNQN) in the data buffer, then the controller shall abort the command with a status code of Invalid Field in Command.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 596, 201, 610]]<|/det|>
If there are:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[142, 618, 820, 666]]<|/det|>
any active controllers in the specified Exported NVM Subsystem; any associations of Exported Namespaces in the specified Exported NVM Subsystem; or any Exported Ports exist in the specified Exported NVM Subsystem,  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 671, 788, 687]]<|/det|>
then the controller shall abort the command with a status code of Command Sequence Error.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 693, 883, 724]]<|/det|>
Upon successful completion of a Manage Exported NVM Subsystem command with a Delete operation the Exported NVM Subsystem identified shall be deleted.  

<|ref|>title<|/ref|><|det|>[[135, 732, 621, 749]]<|/det|>
#### 5.4.9.1.2 Change Access Mode (Management Operation 02h)  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 756, 883, 787]]<|/det|>
The Change Access Mode operation of the Manage Exported NVM Subsystem command is used to change the access mode of an Exported NVM Subsystem to:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[142, 794, 883, 839]]<|/det|>
allow all hosts access to the specified Exported NVM Subsystem; or restrict access to specified hosts listed in the Allowed Host List associated to the specified Exported NVM Subsystem.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 846, 883, 906]]<|/det|>
The data buffer for the Change Access Mode operation of the Manage Exported NVM Subsystem command specifies an NVM Subsystem NQN indicating the Exported NVM Subsystem for which the Access Mode is to be changed. The Management Operation Specific field in Command Dword 10 for the Change Access Mode operation is shown in Figure 556.
