<|ref|>title<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 539, 327, 555]]<|/det|>
#### 8.1.6.3.1.1 Key Derivation  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 563, 883, 595]]<|/det|>
The Derived HMAC Key (DHK) shall be derived by applying a secure keyed- hash function (refer to the CDPALG field in Figure 328) to:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[142, 600, 883, 648]]<|/det|>
the CDP Subsystem Unique String as defined in Figure 654; and the host- specified value of the key (i.e., the key specified in the Host Programmed Key field in the Security Send command payload),  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 653, 883, 684]]<|/det|>
as the inputs to the secure keyed- hash function. If an authentication method is supported (refer to the AUS field in Figure 285), then the FGUID field as defined in Figure 328 shall be supported.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 689, 883, 720]]<|/det|>
The CDP Subsystem Unique String is shown in Figure 654. That string is used by the controller for deriving the DHK that is unique to the NVM subsystem.  

<|ref|>table<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 756, 883, 870]]<|/det|>
<|ref|>table_caption<|/ref|><|det|>[[291, 733, 705, 750]]<|/det|>
Figure 641: CDP Subsystem Unique String Definition   

<table><tr><td>Bytes</td><td>Description</td></tr><tr><td>219:000</td><td>NQN Substring (NQNID): This field contains the NQN substring. This field shall contain bytes 223:4 of the NVM Subsystem NVMe Qualified Name (SUBQNQ) field (refer to Figure 328) (i.e., the SUBQNQ field, excluding the &quot;nqn.&quot; string).</td></tr><tr><td>235:220</td><td>FGUID (FGUID): This field contains the FGUID. This field shall be set to the value of the FRU Globally Unique Identifier (FGUID) field in the Identify Controller data structure.</td></tr><tr><td>255:236</td><td>Serial Number (SN): The field contains the serial number. This field shall be set to the value of the Serial Number (SN) field in the Identify Controller data structure.</td></tr></table>
