<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 413, 831, 429]]<|/det|>
This section defines operations used with the Directive Receive command for the Identify Directive.  

<|ref|>title<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 437, 558, 454]]<|/det|>
#### 8.1.9.2.1.1 Return Parameters (Directive Operation 01h)  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 462, 883, 536]]<|/det|>
This operation returns a data structure that contains a bit vector specifying the Directive Types supported by the controller and a bit vector specifying the Directive Types enabled for the namespace. The data structure returned is defined in Figure 648. If an NSID value of FFFFFFFFh is specified, then the controller shall abort the command with a status code of Invalid Field in Command. The DSPEC field in command Dword 11 is not used for this operation.  

