<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 766, 883, 809]]<|/det|>
Stream identifiers are assigned by the host and may be in the range 0001h to FFFFh. The host may specify a sparse set of stream identifiers (i.e., there is no requirement for the host to use Stream Identifiers in any particular order).

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 818, 883, 889]]<|/det|>
The host may access a namespace through multiple controllers in the NVM subsystem. The controllers in an NVM subsystem indicate in the SSID bit (refer to Figure 655) if a stream identifier is unique based on the Host Identifier (i.e., the same stream identifier used to access the same namespace by a host that has registered a different Host Identifier is referencing a different stream), or if a stream identifier may be used by multiple Host Identifiers (i.e., the same stream identifier used to access the same namespace by a host
