Stream ID 1- a and Stream ID 1- b have the same meaning; Stream ID 1- c has a different meaning; and Stream ID 1- d has a different meaning.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 778, 833, 794]]<|/det|>
In the example shown in Figure 653, if the SSID bit is set to '1', then there is one stream as follows:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[140, 800, 825, 816]]<|/det|>
Stream ID 1- a, Stream ID 1- b, Stream ID 1- c, and Stream ID 1- d have the same meaning.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 822, 883, 852]]<|/det|>
The controller(s) recognized by the NVM subsystem as being associated with a specific host or hosts and attached to a specific namespace either:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 860, 883, 906]]<|/det|>
- utilizes a number of stream resources allocated for exclusive use of that namespace as returned in response to an Allocate Resources operation; or- utilizes resources from the NVM subsystem stream resources.
