<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 530, 883, 576]]<|/det|>
The result of a Namespace Management command that creates a namespace within the Endurance Group is that at least one Placement Handle is defined for that namespace (refer to the Namespace Management section in applicable NVM Express I/O Command Set specification).  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 582, 883, 628]]<|/det|>
For any namespace created in an Endurance Group that has Flexible Data Placement enabled, the host may issue an I/O Management Receive command to obtain a list of Placement Handles and the associated Reclaim Unit Handles that are used by the Data Placement Directive in write commands.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 633, 839, 650]]<|/det|>
If the Flexible Data Placement capability is supported, then the controller shall support the following:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[142, 655, 883, 831]]<|/det|>
a) the Feature Identifiers Supported and Effects log page (refer to section 5.2.12.1.18); 
b) the I/O Management Receive command (refer to section 7.3) and the Reclaim Unit Handle Status Management Operation in that command (refer to Figure 595); 
c) the I/O Management Send command (refer to section 7.4) and the Placement Identifier Update Management Operation in that command (refer to Figure 599); 
d) the Flexible Data Placement feature (refer to section 5.2.26.1.20); 
e) the FDP Configurations log page (refer to section 5.2.12.1.29); 
f) the Reclaim Unit Handle Usage log page (refer to section 5.2.12.1.30); 
g) the FDP Statistics log page (refer to section 5.2.12.1.31); 
h) the Flexible Data Placement Events feature (refer to section 5.2.26.1.21); 
i) the FDP Events log page (refer to section 5.2.12.1.32); and 
j) the Data Placement Directive (refer to section 8.1.9.4).  

<|ref|>title<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 838, 552, 854]]<|/det|>
#### 8.1.11.2 Enabling Flexible Data Placement (Informative)  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 863, 883, 894]]<|/det|>
The host prepares an Endurance Group for operation in Flexible Data Placement using the following process:
2025-12-21 11:28:00 - ocr_processor - [32mINFO[0m - [deepseek_ocr.py:175] - Processing image start: out/output_png/0597_page.png
2025-12-21 11:28:06 - ocr_processor - [32mINFO[0m - [deepseek_ocr.py:182] - Processing image end: <|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 88, 883, 134]]<|/det|>
1) Validate that the Flexible Data Placement capability is supported by issuing an Identify command to access the Identify Controller data structure and checking that the Flexible Data Placement Support (FDPS) bit is set to '1'.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 133, 883, 163]]<|/det|>
2) Delete any existing namespaces that exist in the Endurance Group where Flexible Data Placement is to be enabled.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 163, 883, 206]]<|/det|>
3) Issue a Get Log Page command specifying the FDP Configurations log page (refer to section 5.2.12.1.29). Parse the FDP Configurations List in the returned log page to determine the desired FDP configuration.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 205, 883, 235]]<|/det|>
4) Enable Flexible Data Placement utilizing that desired FDP configuration by issuing a Set Features command specifying:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[202, 242, 883, 330]]<|/det|>
a. the Flexible Data Placement feature; 
b. the Endurance Group Identifier field set to the ENDGID of the Endurance Group in which Flexible Data Placement is to be enabled; 
c. the FDPE bit set to '1' (i.e., enabling Flexible Data Placement); and 
d. the Flexible Data Placement Configuration Index field set to the index of the desired FDP configuration from the FDP Configurations List in the FDP Configurations log page.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 336, 883, 366]]<|/det|>
5) Issue an Identify command specifying the Identify Namespace data structure (i.e., CNS 00h as defined in Figure 326) to identify which LBA formats are supported.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 366, 883, 396]]<|/det|>
6) For each namespace to be created in the Endurance Group, issue a Namespace Management command (refer to section 5.2.21) specifying:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[202, 402, 883, 476]]<|/det|>
a. the Select field set to the Create operation; 
b. the User Data Format; and 
c. the Placement Handle List used to define the Reclaim Unit Handle associated with each Placement Handle of the namespace (refer to the Namespace Management section of the applicable NVM Express I/O Command Set specification).  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 482, 883, 512]]<|/det|>
7) Issue Get Features commands for the FDP Events feature (refer to section 5.2.26.1.21) to acquire the list of supported FDP events and the enabled state of each supported FDP event.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 511, 883, 541]]<|/det|>
8) Issue Set Features commands for the FDP Events feature (refer to section 5.2.26.1.21) to specify if FDP events are required for Reclaim Unit Handles.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 541, 883, 571]]<|/det|>
9) For each namespace created in an Endurance Group in which the Data Placement Directive is to be utilized by the host by write commands specifying that namespace:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[202, 577, 556, 592]]<|/det|>
a. Issue a Directive Send command specifying:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[259, 599, 859, 673]]<|/det|>
i. the Directive Operation field set to Enable Directive (i.e., 01h); ii. the NSID of that namespace; iii. the DTYPE field in Command Dword 11 set to Identify (i.e., 00h); iv. the DTYPE field in Command Dword 12 set to Data Placement (i.e., 02h); and v. the Enable Directive bit set to '1' (i.e., to enable the Data Placement Directive).  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[202, 680, 883, 724]]<|/det|>
b. Issue an Identify command with CNS value 08h (i.e., the I/O Command Set Independent Identify Namespace data structure) to determine if a volatile write cache is present for the namespace.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[116, 730, 883, 760]]<|/det|>
Following a Controller Level Reset, the host performs the following actions before resuming use of Flexible Data Placement in an Endurance Group:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[145, 766, 419, 782]]<|/det|>
1) Determine the FDP configuration:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[202, 789, 883, 862]]<|/det|>
a. Issue a Get Feature command specifying the Flexible Data Placement feature (i.e., 1Dh) and the ENDGID for the Endurance Group to determine if Flexible Data Placement is enabled and the Flexible Data Placement Configuration Index. 
b. Issue a Get Log Page command specifying the FDP Configurations log page (i.e., Log Page Identifier 20h).  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 869, 883, 899]]<|/det|>
2) Issue Get Features commands for the FDP Events feature (refer to section 5.2.26.1.21) to acquire the list of supported FDP events and the enabled state of each supported FDP event.
