<|ref|>title<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 640, 281, 656]]<|/det|>
#### 8.1.18.6 Power Limit  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 664, 883, 696]]<|/det|>
Controller support for the Power Limit capability is indicated by the Power Limit Support (PLS) bit in the Controller Attributes (CTRATT) field of the Identify Controller data structure (refer to Figure 328).  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 701, 883, 776]]<|/det|>
The Power Limit capability enables a host to limit the maximum power consumed by the NVM subsystem by restricting the power states that each controller is permitted to use. The host is able to use the Power Management capability to configure the power state of a controller and is able to use the Power Limit capability to prohibit controller power states that allow the NVM subsystem to consume more power than a power limit that the host specifies.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 782, 883, 828]]<|/det|>
The host is able to modify the power limit for a controller by using the Set Features command to change the attributes of the Power Limit feature (refer to section 5.2.26.1.25). The host is able to obtain the current power limit for a controller by using the Get Features command to read the attributes of that Feature.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 833, 883, 879]]<|/det|>
The power limit indicated by the Power Limit feature prohibits power states that allow consumption of more power than the power limit (i.e., power states for which the power consumption allowed by the value of the MP field in the PSD data structure (refer to Figure 329) is greater than the power limit).
