<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 412, 883, 442]]<|/det|>
If an interval power measurement is reported in the Interval Power Measurement (IPM) field in the SMART / Health Information log page, then interval power measurements shall be collected for that field.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 449, 883, 494]]<|/det|>
If the cumulative operational energy consumed is reported in the Operational Lifetime Energy Consumed (OLEC) field in the SMART / Health Information log page, then interval power measurements shall be collected for that field.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 500, 883, 531]]<|/det|>
The collection of interval power measurements for the Power Threshold feature and Power Measurement capability are dependent on whether the respective capabilities are enabled.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 537, 133, 550]]<|/det|>
If:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 560, 883, 650]]<|/det|>
- an interval power measurement is reported in the Interval Power Measurement (IPM) field in the SMART / Health Information log page;- the cumulative operational energy consumed is reported in the Operational Lifetime Energy Consumed (OLEC) field in the SMART / Health Information log page;- the Power Threshold feature is supported; or- the Power Measurement capability is supported,  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 657, 883, 688]]<|/det|>
then the controller shall set the Interval Power Measurement Sample Rate (IPMSR) field in the Identify Controller data structure (refer to Figure 328) to a non-zero value.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 694, 428, 709]]<|/det|>
Figure 681 defines the power scale for the:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 717, 675, 794]]<|/det|>
- Interval Power Scale (IPS) field (refer to Figure 158);- Average Interval Power Scale (AIPWRS) field (refer to Figure 297);- Maximum Interval Power Scale (MIPWRS) field (refer to Figure 297);- Power Scale (PWRS) field (refer to Figure 298); and- Power Threshold Scale (PTS) field (refer to Figure 453).  

