2025-12-21 11:35:21 - ocr_processor - [32mINFO[0m - [deepseek_ocr.py:182] - Processing image end: <|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 89, 883, 120]]<|/det|>
If a sanitize operation includes deallocation of all media in the sanitization target that is allocated for user data, then that deallocation shall be performed in exactly one of the following states:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 127, 434, 173]]<|/det|>
Restricted Processing state; Unrestricted Processing state; or Post- Verification Deallocation state.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 179, 790, 195]]<|/det|>
If the command (refer to Figure 388 and Figure 391) that starts a sanitize operation specified:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 202, 603, 249]]<|/det|>
the Enter Media Verification State (EMVS) bit cleared to '0'; the AUSE bit cleared to '0'; and the No- Deallocate After Sanitize (NDAS) bit, if any:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[202, 256, 883, 315]]<|/det|>
cleared to '0'; or set to '1' and the controller encounters a condition that results in unexpected deallocation of all media in the sanitization target that is allocated for user data (refer to section 5.2.26.1.15),  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 320, 883, 351]]<|/det|>
then deallocation of all media in the sanitization target that is allocated for user data shall be performed in the Restricted Processing state. If that deallocation fails, then sanitize processing fails.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 356, 883, 402]]<|/det|>
If Media Verification state is canceled (i.e., the MVCNCLD bit is set to '1') during the Restricted Processing state, then deallocation of all media in the sanitization target that is allocated for user data shall be performed in the Restricted Processing state.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 408, 525, 424]]<|/det|>
If the command that starts a sanitize operation specifies:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 430, 603, 476]]<|/det|>
the Enter Media Verification State (EMVS) bit cleared to '0'; the AUSE bit set to '1'; and the No- Deallocate After Sanitize (NDAS) bit, if any:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[202, 484, 883, 543]]<|/det|>
cleared to '0'; or set to '1' and the controller encounters a condition that results in unexpected deallocation of all media in the sanitization target that is allocated for user data (refer to section 5.2.26.1.15),  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 549, 883, 580]]<|/det|>
then deallocation of all media in the sanitization target that is allocated for user data shall be performed in the Unrestricted Processing state. If that deallocation fails, then sanitize processing fails.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 585, 883, 630]]<|/det|>
If the Media Verification state is canceled (i.e., the MVCNCLD bit is set to '1') during the Unrestricted Processing state, then deallocation of all media in the sanitization target that is allocated for user data shall be performed in the Unrestricted Processing state.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 637, 698, 653]]<|/det|>
In the Post- Verification Deallocation state the controller deallocates all user data.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 659, 538, 674]]<|/det|>
In the Post- Verification Deallocation state, if the controller:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 682, 883, 757]]<|/det|>
successfully completes deallocating all media in the sanitization target that is allocated for user data, then the sanitization target enters the Idle state; or fails to deallocate all media in the sanitization target that is allocated for user data, then the sanitization target enters the Restricted Failure state or the Unrestricted Failure state, as described in section 8.1.26.4.7.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 763, 883, 793]]<|/det|>
A Controller Level Reset may cause the sanitize operation not to include the Media Verification state and the Post- Verification Deallocation state, as described in section 8.1.26.4.  

<|ref|>title<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 801, 484, 818]]<|/det|>
#### 8.1.26.3 Sanitize Operation Types and Support  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 826, 883, 857]]<|/det|>
The Sanitize Capabilities (SANICAP) field of the Identify Controller data structure (refer to Figure 328) indicates the sanitize operation types supported and controller attributes specific to sanitize operations.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[116, 863, 354, 878]]<|/det|>
The sanitize operation types are:
2025-12-21 11:35:23 - ocr_processor - [32mINFO[0m - [deepseek_ocr.py:175] - Processing image start: out/output_png/0658_page.png
2025-12-21 11:35:28 - ocr_processor - [32mINFO[0m - [deepseek_ocr.py:182] - Processing image end: <|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 90, 883, 210]]<|/det|>
- the Block Erase sanitize operation, which alters user data with a low-level block erase method that is specific to the media for all locations on the media within the sanitization target in which user data may be stored;- the Crypto Erase sanitize operation, which alters user data by changing the media encryption keys for all locations on the media within the sanitization target in which user data may be stored; and- the Overwrite sanitize operation, which alters user data by writing a fixed data pattern or related patterns one or more times to all locations on the media within the sanitization target in which user data may be stored. Figure 705 defines the data pattern or patterns that are written.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 216, 667, 232]]<|/det|>
Controller attributes that affect the processing of sanitize operations include:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 237, 883, 416]]<|/det|>
- the No-Deallocate Modifies Media After Sanitize (NODMMAS) field, which indicates whether media is modified by the controller as part of sanitize processing for an NVM subsystem sanitize operation and that had been requested with the No-Deallocate After Sanitize (NDAS) bit set to '1' in the Sanitize command that started the NVM subsystem sanitize operation;- the No-Deallocate Inhibited (NDI) bit, which indicates if the controller supports the No-Deallocate After Sanitize bit in the Sanitize command;- the Verification Support (VERS) bit, which indicates if the controller supports the Media Verification state and the Post-Verification Deallocation state for NVM subsystem sanitize operations that perform block erase or crypto erase; and- the Namespace Verification Support (NVERS) bit, which indicates if the controller supports the Media Verification state and the Post-Verification Deallocation state for namespace sanitize operations.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 421, 883, 482]]<|/det|>
If the NODMMAS field indicates a value of 10b in the Identify Controller data structure (refer to Figure 328) and a Sanitize command that starts an NVM subsystem sanitize operation specifies the No- Deallocate After Sanitize (NDAS) bit set to '1', then sanitize processing includes additional media modification. Refer to Annex A.3 for further information about sanitize operations and interactions with integrity circuits.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 487, 883, 532]]<|/det|>
The Overwrite sanitize operation is media specific and may not be appropriate for all media types. For example, if the media is NAND, multiple pass overwrite operations may have an adverse effect on media endurance.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 538, 883, 598]]<|/det|>
If the NVM subsystem supports the Key Per I/O capability (refer to section 8.1.14), then a sanitize operation shall alter all user data such that recovery of any previous user data using the KEYTAG values specified when that previous user data was written (i.e., original KEYTAG values) is infeasible for a given level of effort (refer to ISO/IEC 27040).  

