<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[222, 703, 882, 730]]<|/det|>
ii. set the Namespace Data Erased (NDE) bit to '1' in the Sanitize Status log page for each namespace that exists in the NVM subsystem; and

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[216, 732, 882, 759]]<|/det|>
iii. set the SANS field to Oh (i.e., Idle state) in the Sanitize Status log page for the NVM subsystem and each namespace that exists in the NVM subsystem;

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[144, 768, 470, 781]]<|/det|>
b) if the sanitization target is a namespace:

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[173, 790, 882, 817]]<|/det|>
o set the Namespace Data Erased (NDE) bit to '1' in the Sanitize Status log page for that namespace; and

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[173, 820, 867, 832]]<|/det|>
o set the SANS field to Oh (i.e., Idle state) in the Sanitize Status log page for that namespace;

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[173, 842, 206, 853]]<|/det|>
and

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[144, 864, 858, 876]]<|/det|>
c) report the Sanitize Operation Completed asynchronous event as described in section 8.1.26.1.

