<|ref|>title<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 260, 430, 276]]<|/det|>
#### 8.1.26.5 Sanitize Operation Restrictions  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 284, 279, 300]]<|/det|>
In the following states:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 308, 394, 400]]<|/det|>
Restricted Processing; Restricted Failure; Unrestricted Processing; Unrestricted Failure; Media Verification; and Post- Verification Deallocation,  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 406, 883, 437]]<|/det|>
all enabled controllers in the NVM subsystem have restrictions in the set of actions that they are allowed to perform.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 443, 883, 488]]<|/det|>
When a sanitize operation starts on any controller (i.e., a transition into the Restricted Processing state occurs or a transition into the Unrestricted Processing state occurs), all controllers in the NVM subsystem shall:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 495, 834, 541]]<|/det|>
update the Sanitize Status log page for the sanitization target (refer to section 5.2.12.1.36); suspend autonomous power state management activities as described in section 8.1.18.2; for NVM subsystem sanitize operations:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[173, 547, 880, 666]]<|/det|>
clear all of the following outstanding asynchronous events: Sanitize Operation Completed asynchronous event, if any; Sanitize Operation Completed With Unexpected Deallocation asynchronous event, if any; and Sanitize Operation Entered Media Verification State asynchronous event, if any;  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[173, 666, 590, 708]]<|/det|>
abort any command (submitted or in progress) not allowed during an NVM subsystem sanitize operation (refer to Figure 143) with a status code of Sanitize In Progress, unless otherwise specified (e.g., a media verification Read command);  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[173, 703, 550, 717]]<|/det|>
release stream identifiers for any open streams;  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[173, 722, 204, 735]]<|/det|>
and  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 741, 880, 848]]<|/det|>
for namespace sanitize operations: abort any I/O command (submitted or in progress) specifying the NSID of the namespace, unless otherwise specified (e.g., a media verification Read command); process any Admin command as specified in section 5.1.2; abort any in progress device self-test operations specifying the NSID of the namespace or specifying the NSID set to FFFFFFFFh; and release stream identifiers allocated for exclusive use by the namespace for any open streams.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 855, 647, 871]]<|/det|>
If a sanitize operation is in any of the following states (i.e., is in progress):  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 878, 340, 893]]<|/det|>
Restricted Processing;
2025-12-21 11:37:11 - ocr_processor - [32mINFO[0m - [deepseek_ocr.py:175] - Processing image start: out/output_png/0673_page.png
2025-12-21 11:40:20 - ocr_processor - [32mINFO[0m - [deepseek_ocr.py:182] - Processing image end: <|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[144, 91, 394, 136]]<|/det|>
- Unrestricted Processing;- Media Verification; or- Post-Verification Deallocation,  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 143, 457, 158]]<|/det|>
then for each controller in the NVM subsystem:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[144, 166, 597, 211]]<|/det|>
