#### 8.3.2.3 Fabric Zoning  

<|ref|>title<|/ref|><|det|>[[137, 500, 270, 516]]<|/det|>
#### 8.3.2.3.1 Model  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 524, 883, 600]]<|/det|>
A Centralized Discovery controller (CDC) may provide centralized access control services (i.e., Fabric Zoning) for an NVMe- oF IP- based fabric. CDC- based Fabric Zoning provides a way to control the Discovery log pages provided in response to a Get Log Page command issued to the CDC. Fabric Zoning should be based on a Zoning database maintained by the CDC and containing two fundamental data structures: the ZoneDBConfig and the ZoneDBActive, as shown in Figure 737.  

<|ref|>image<|/ref|><|det|>[[242, 640, 753, 800]]<|/det|>
<|ref|>image_caption<|/ref|><|det|>[[311, 612, 684, 629]]<|/det|>
<center>Figure 737: Zoning DB Abstract Representation </center>  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 814, 740, 831]]<|/det|>
The ZoneDBActive is a list of enforced ZoneGroups. The enforcement actions include:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[143, 838, 845, 886]]<|/det|>
Discovery log page filtering; Discovery Log Page Change Asynchronous Event notifications (refer to section 8.3.2.4); and optionally, network level restrictions (refer to section 8.3.2.3.5.2).  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 891, 643, 908]]<|/det|>
The abstract representation of the ZoneDBActive is shown in Figure 738.
