<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 432, 728, 445]]<|/det|>
The members of a Zone may communicate with each other using the following rules:

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[144, 456, 523, 468]]<|/det|>
· hosts may communicate with NVM subsystems;

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[144, 472, 523, 483]]<|/det|>
· NVM subsystems may communicate with hosts;

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[144, 487, 494, 498]]<|/det|>
· hosts shall not communicate with hosts; and

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[144, 502, 640, 514]]<|/det|>
· NVM subsystems shall not communicate with NVM subsystems.

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 522, 883, 579]]<|/det|>
A Zone of a ZoneGroup belonging to the ZoneDBConfig may use all defined Zone member types. When a ZoneGroup belonging to the ZoneDBConfig is activated and becomes part of the ZoneDBActive, all ZoneAlias name Zone members are resolved in the group of NVMe entities referenced by the ZoneAlias name.

<|ref|>sub_title<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 591, 537, 604]]<|/det|>
## 8.3.2.3.4.2 {NQN, Role} Zone Member Type (Type 1h)

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[114, 615, 883, 656]]<|/det|>
This Zone member type identifies all fabric interfaces, all IP protocols (e.g., TCP or UDP), and all IP protocol ports (e.g., TCP port 4420) that may be used by the NVMe-oF entity identified by the Zone member's NQN.The format of this Zone member type is shown in Figure 743.

<|ref|>table_caption<|/ref|><|det|>[[318, 674, 679, 686]]<|/det|>
